# M2b: throughput repair for the M2a on-line subsumption prototype,
# plus the cross-bound prune M2a's report made a pre-condition for n>=11.
#
# Applies on top of, in order:
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-macos-proc.patch
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-instrumentation-v3.patch
#   tools/patches/sortnetopt-online-subsumption-v3.patch
# against the pinned upstream commit 0b5d09c47446096f9e3a0812b35afc72b7f2a718.
# Apply with:  patch -V none -p1 -i <this file>
#
# The Isabelle/HOL-extracted checker (checker/) is not touched.
#
# Three structural changes, in the order the M2a profile ranked their cost:
#
#  1. src/search/subsume.rs (new) - the per-width on-line subsumption index is
#     partitioned into one OutputSetIndex, with its own RwLock, per value of
#     |set| (the popcount of the packed bitmap). Permutation and complement are
#     bijections of the Boolean cube, so subsumption is cardinality-monotone:
#     a lookup for Q need only visit buckets 0..=|Q| and the eviction pass of
#     an insert of A need only visit buckets |A|+1..  . Exact - a skipped
#     bucket provably contains no entry in a subsumption relation with the
#     query. This is simultaneously the fix for the single per-width RwLock
#     (M2a: ~17 % of thread time) and for the k-d traversal (M2a: ~31 %).
#     Query monotonicity under sharding is re-established by inserting before
#     evicting and by scanning buckets in DESCENDING popcount order; the
#     argument is in the module documentation.
#
#  2. src/output_set/index.rs - OutputSetIndex::lookup_with_abstraction_from,
#     a seeded variant of lookup_with_abstraction. Restarting the
#     best-so-far accumulator in every bucket destroys the value-range pruning
#     that keeps subsumes_permuted off the hot path; threading it through
#     restores it (measured 6.4 s -> 3.6 s of the n=9 search-phase wall).
#     Also OutputSetIndex::remove_dominated_with_abstraction, the eviction half
#     of insert_with_abstraction_collect, extracted verbatim.
#
#  3. src/output_set/index.rs - LowerInvert::test_precise now guards its
#     complement branch with that branch's own abstraction test. Upstream
#     guards only the identity branch and then runs the complemented
#     subsumes_permuted unconditionally; subsumes_permuted is ~61 % of active
#     thread time. Exact: complementing an output set acts on its abstraction
#     as the coordinate permutation i^3, so the guard is precisely the
#     invert=1 disjunct of LowerInvert::test_abstraction that the caller has
#     already allowed for.
#
# Plus, gated and off by default:
#
#  4. src/prune.rs - prune_all_cross_bound, enabled by
#     SORTNETOPT_CROSS_BOUND_PRUNE=1. Drops A at bound b whenever some
#     same-width Y with bound(Y) >= b subsumes A, processing ascending in
#     |set| and never dropping the root. With the variable unset, prune_all is
#     byte-for-byte the upstream per-group prune.
#
#     One robustness fix travels with it, in src/proof.rs: gen_proof mmaps
#     every .pbin listed in index.txt, and memmap refuses a zero-length
#     mapping. The per-group prune can never empty a group (its smallest-|set|
#     record has nothing in its own index to be subsumed by), but the
#     cross-bound prune can, so such a group is now skipped. Behaviour is
#     unchanged whenever no group is empty, and an empty group contributes no
#     entries either way. checker/ is still untouched.
#
# Environment variables are otherwise unchanged from the M2a patch.
